name><surname>Miglioretti</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Hormone therapy prescribing patterns in the United States</article-title><source>Obstet Gynecol</source><year>2004</year><volume>104</volume><issue>5 Pt 1</issue><fpage>1042</fpage><lpage>1050</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Buist DS, Newton KM, Miglioretti DL, et al. Hormone therapy prescribing patterns in the United States. Obstet Gynecol. 2004;104(5 Pt 1):1042&#x02013;50. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15516400</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR5"><label>5.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Phillips</surname><given-names>DP</given-names></name><name><surname>Kanter</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Bednarczyk</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Tastad</surname><given-names>PL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Importance of the lay press in the transmission of medical knowledge to the scientific community</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><year>1991</year><volume>325</volume><issue>16</issue><fpage>1180</fpage><lpage>1183</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Phillips DP, Kanter EJ, Bednarczyk B, Tastad PL. Importance of the lay press in the transmission of medical knowledge to the scientific community. N Engl J Med. 1991;325(16):1180&#x02013;3. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1891034</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR6"><label>6.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Shattuck lecture-medicine and the media</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><year>1998</year><volume>339</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>87</fpage><lpage>92</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1056/NEJM199807093390206</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Johnson T. Shattuck lecture-medicine and the media. N Engl J Med. 1998;339(2):87&#x02013;92. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9654540</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR7"><label>7.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Newton</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Lacroix</surname><given-names>AZ</given-names></name><name><surname>Leveille</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name><name><surname>Rutter</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Keenan</surname><given-names>NL</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The physician&#x02019;s role in women&#x02019;s decision making about hormone replacement therapy</article-title><source>Obstet Gynecol</source><year>1998</year><volume>92</volume><issue>4 Pt 1</issue><fpage>580</fpage><lpage>584</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0029-7844(98)00272-5</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Newton KM, Lacroix AZ, Leveille SG, Rutter C, Keenan NL, Anderson LA. The physician&#x02019;s role in women&#x02019;s decision making about hormone replacement therapy. Obstet Gynecol. 1998;92(4 Pt 1):580&#x02013;4. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9764632</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR8"><label>8.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McIntosh</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Blalock</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effects of media coverage of Women&#x02019;s Health Initiative study on attitudes and behavior of women receiving hormone replacement therapy</article-title><source>Am J Health Syst Pharm</source><year>2005</year><volume>62</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>69</fpage><lpage>74</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">McIntosh J, Blalock SJ. Effects of